Note: Test octave N { ... } block — quick-260702-gmm default-octave musical-context block.
Note:
Note: Bare note letters inside a | ... | stream adopt the block's octave (C -> C3 inside
Note: octave 3). Explicit octave digits always win. Nesting is innermost-wins; scope reverts
Note: to octave 4 after the block; dynamic scope reaches note streams inside called procs.
Note: Out-of-range octave N clamps charitably to [1, 9] with a one-shot [octave] advisory.
Note:
Note: HARNESS: uses the @test framework's `assertNotesMatch`, which compares Sequences
Note: structurally INCLUDING octave — `str` of a Sequence only shows a bar/beat summary
Note: (not pitch), so a plain (equals (str a) (str b)) can NOT distinguish octaves. Run with:
Note:   dotnet run --project flow-cli -- test tests/test_octave_block.flow
Note: Emits PASS/FAIL lines + a Total/Passed/Failed summary; exits non-zero on any FAIL.
Note:
Note: Sequences are built inside helper procs because an `octave N { ... }` block creates its
Note: own variable scope (locals do not leak out) — a proc `return`s the sequence built under
Note: the block. Reference sequences use explicit octave digits (which the block never affects).
Note:
Note: SCOPE NOTE: a bare `Note n = C;` OUTSIDE a note stream still defaults to octave 4 — the
Note: lexer has no musical context at that point (locked scope decision). Only note-stream bare
Note: letters (main notes, bracket chords, ghost/grace, tuplet notes) follow the octave block.
use "@std"
use "@test"

Note: ===== Helper procs: build note streams under octave blocks and return them =====

Note: bare letters at octave 3
proc bare3()
    octave 3 { return | C D E | }
end proc

Note: explicit octave digits inside an octave-3 block (should stay 5)
proc explicitIn3()
    octave 3 { return | C5 D5 | }
end proc

Note: bracket chord with bare letters at octave 3
proc bracket3()
    octave 3 { return | [C E G]q | }
end proc

Note: ghost + grace bare notes at octave 3
proc ghostGrace3()
    octave 3 { return | (ghost C) (grace D) E | }
end proc

Note: nested blocks — innermost (2) wins over outer (5)
proc nested52()
    octave 5 { octave 2 { return | C | } }
end proc

Note: code AFTER a block reverts to the default octave 4
proc afterBlock()
    octave 2 { Sequence discard = | C | (print) }
    return | C |
end proc

Note: a note stream built by a proc with NO octave block of its own —
Note: it must inherit the CALLER's octave via dynamic scope (like tempo/swing)
proc makeSeq()
    return | C D E |
end proc

proc dynamicScope3()
    octave 3 { return (makeSeq) }
end proc

Note: out-of-range octave clamps charitably to 9 (also emits a one-shot [octave] advisory)
proc clamp12()
    octave 12 { return | C | }
end proc

Note: ===== Reference sequences (explicit octaves — the octave block never touches these) =====
Sequence ref3 = | C3 D3 E3 |
Sequence ref5 = | C5 D5 |
Sequence rcChord = | [C3 E3 G3]q |
Sequence refGhostGrace3 = | (ghost C3) (grace D3) E3 |
Sequence r2 = | C2 |
Sequence refC4 = | C4 |
Sequence ref9 = | C9 |

Note: ===== Assertions =====
(test "bare letters adopt octave 3" lazy((assertNotesMatch (bare3) ref3)))
(test "explicit octave digits win over block default" lazy((assertNotesMatch (explicitIn3) ref5)))
(test "bracket chord bare notes adopt octave 3" lazy((assertNotesMatch (bracket3) rcChord)))
(test "ghost + grace bare notes adopt octave 3" lazy((assertNotesMatch (ghostGrace3) refGhostGrace3)))
(test "innermost octave wins in nested blocks" lazy((assertNotesMatch (nested52) r2)))
(test "bare note reverts to octave 4 after block" lazy((assertNotesMatch (afterBlock) refC4)))
(test "proc note stream inherits caller octave (dynamic scope)" lazy((assertNotesMatch (dynamicScope3) ref3)))
(test "octave 12 clamps to 9" lazy((assertNotesMatch (clamp12) ref9)))
